(7548042, 1208675, 62357, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7 but have to say the processing let it down for me.  If it looked as good as on the Spark you just shared, I''m sure it would have done tons better.</td>', 'I gave this a 7 but have to say the processing let it down for me.  If it looked as good as on the Spark you just shared, I''m sure it would have done tons better.', '2017-12-11 06:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548052, 1208837, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>A lovely golden hour seascape Janine. Though the sky and the foreground beach have some interest it is difficult to favour one over the other for compositional purposes which may be the reason it didnt score higher. In this situation I will usually try and emphasise one over the other and more often than not I will choose the foreground, in this sort of situation I think this would have improved it and your result here but we will never know. Anyway, lovely image thanks for sharing.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well A lovely golden hour seascape Janine. Though the sky and the foreground beach have some interest it is difficult to favour one over the other for compositional purposes which may be the reason it didnt score higher. In this situation I will usually try and emphasise one over the other and more often than not I will choose the foreground, in this sort of situation I think this would have improved it and your result here but we will never know. Anyway, lovely image thanks for sharing.', '2017-12-11 09:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548053, 1208778, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>A well composed landscape that makes you feel a part of the scene in front of you. I like the duality of the foreground rocks with the background mountains, also the foreground detail of the water, its nice that you havent gone for the overdone cliched effect of over blurring it makes a now pleasant change. As with any good landscape they dont just magically happen they are well thought out and executed in the perfect light and thats what this image is all about it has all the hallmarks of someone who knows how to get the most out of their surroundings, well done Kees</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well A well composed landscape that makes you feel a part of the scene in front of you. I like the duality of the foreground rocks with the background mountains, also the foreground detail of the water, its nice that you havent gone for the overdone cliched effect of over blurring it makes a now pleasant change. As with any good landscape they dont just magically happen they are well thought out and executed in the perfect light and thats what this image is all about it has all the hallmarks of someone who knows how to get the most out of their surroundings, well done Kees', '2017-12-11 10:06:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548055, 1208730, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Hes a fine handsome young chap. Youve got a nice good sharp focus on his eyes which, as you already know, is essential for any portrait, this together with the shallow DOF helps retain our focus on him and this all works well. Personally, I think I would have tried to get a little lower down to his level, it is usually a more engaging end result rather than looking down on him. What spoils the image for me is the bright light on the top of his head, there are some clear areas there of overexposure which is a real shame especially in such a crucial area, his lovely blonde hair should be glowingly clothing his head like a crown.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Hes a fine handsome young chap. Youve got a nice good sharp focus on his eyes which, as you already know, is essential for any portrait, this together with the shallow DOF helps retain our focus on him and this all works well. Personally, I think I would have tried to get a little lower down to his level, it is usually a more engaging end result rather than looking down on him. What spoils the image for me is the bright light on the top of his head, there are some clear areas there of overexposure which is a real shame especially in such a crucial area, his lovely blonde hair should be glowingly clothing his head like a crown.', '2017-12-11 10:19:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548056, 1208811, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Congratulations for your deserved high score and HM for this excellent image. Its all in the detail, truly amazing, theyre insects that we either love or loath but when you are able to see them like this difficult not to be impressed with the way they fit in to the bigger natural picture. Technically its very well executed, the focus is exactly where it should be and I like the slightly off-centre composition. All in all a great image Roger, well done</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Congratulations for your deserved high score and HM for this excellent image. Its all in the detail, truly amazing, theyre insects that we either love or loath but when you are able to see them like this difficult not to be impressed with the way they fit in to the bigger natural picture. Technically its very well executed, the focus is exactly where it should be and I like the slightly off-centre composition. All in all a great image Roger, well done', '2017-12-11 10:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548057, 1208682, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Well done Ronnie, you were well rewarded for waiting in the right position. That is a part of the effort that goes in to your lovely images there is a lot of patient preparation, stalking and waiting for the right moment to get that extraordinary image that stands out from the rest of the crowd.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Well done Ronnie, you were well rewarded for waiting in the right position. That is a part of the effort that goes in to your lovely images there is a lot of patient preparation, stalking and waiting for the right moment to get that extraordinary image that stands out from the rest of the crowd.', '2017-12-11 10:33:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548058, 1208446, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Congratulations Marko for your ribbon, very well deserved for such remarkable image. What really makes the image is the tremendous detail from the lovely sharp focus together with the shallow DOF that helps it really stand out. Your composition is spot on, I love the surrounding foliage it is all so convincing. I think there is a very slight tendency towards over-sharpening but it really does not deter, it certainly shouldnt be confused with the lovely rim lighting on his back. A great image thanks for sharing.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Congratulations Marko for your ribbon, very well deserved for such remarkable image. What really makes the image is the tremendous detail from the lovely sharp focus together with the shallow DOF that helps it really stand out. Your composition is spot on, I love the surrounding foliage it is all so convincing. I think there is a very slight tendency towards over-sharpening but it really does not deter, it certainly shouldnt be confused with the lovely rim lighting on his back. A great image thanks for sharing.', '2017-12-11 10:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548059, 1208400, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Its truly remarkable how much is condensed into so small a space here. It gives us a fascinating insight into the density of the area especially effective at night with all the different lighting and colours. I particularly like the blurred boat on the water in the background. Thanks for shareing this man made world with us Gin.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Its truly remarkable how much is condensed into so small a space here. It gives us a fascinating insight into the density of the area especially effective at night with all the different lighting and colours. I particularly like the blurred boat on the water in the background. Thanks for shareing this man made world with us Gin.', '2017-12-11 10:51:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548061, 1208811, 185773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> sinister and beautiful </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Mariuca,<br/>           I wish I can crop more and bring the subject nearer but I really like the effect ot the web too. Thank you for your comment.<br/> <br/>Best regards,<br/> <br/>Roger New</td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: sinister and beautiful   Hi Mariuca,           I wish I can crop more and bring the subject nearer but I really like the effect ot the web too. Thank you for your comment. Best regards, Roger New', '2017-12-11 10:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548062, 1208811, 185773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ammie:</b></div><hr/><i> Real good job. Congrats </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Ammie,<br/>         I am really glad that it turn out great, the spider is missing a leg and the web has been disturbed, otherwise the symmetry will work better composing the spider in the middle. Thank you for you compliment.<br/> <br/>Best regards,<br/> <br/>Roger New</td>', 'Originally posted by Ammie: Real good job. Congrats   Hi Ammie,         I am really glad that it turn out great, the spider is missing a leg and the web has been disturbed, otherwise the symmetry will work better composing the spider in the middle. Thank you for you compliment. Best regards, Roger New', '2017-12-11 11:01:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548063, 1208811, 185773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Chris_Ang:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats Roger! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Chris,<br/>         Thank you.<br/>Best regards,<br/> <br/>Roger New<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Chris_Ang: Congrats Roger!   Hi Chris,         Thank you.Best regards, Roger New', '2017-12-11 11:03:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548065, 1208811, 185773, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sidpixel:</b></div><hr/><i> Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Congratulations for your deserved high score and HM for this excellent image. Its all in the detail, truly amazing, theyre insects that we either love or loath but when you are able to see them like this difficult not to be impressed with the way they fit in to the bigger natural picture. Technically its very well executed, the focus is exactly where it should be and I like the slightly off-centre composition. All in all a great image Roger, well done </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hi Sidpixel,<br/>            I am just happy to reached the top ten, I place the spider off center for two reasons. One, it is missing a leg thus will not be ideal for composing a symmetry composition. Two, the web which supposed to compliment the spider has been disturbed thus I decided to composed it off center. Thank you so much for you detail comment, it load of help... Appreciated.<br/> <br/>Best regards,<br/> <br/>Roger New<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-12-11 11:11:45.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by sidpixel: Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Congratulations for your deserved high score and HM for this excellent image. Its all in the detail, truly amazing, theyre insects that we either love or loath but when you are able to see them like this difficult not to be impressed with the way they fit in to the bigger natural picture. Technically its very well executed, the focus is exactly where it should be and I like the slightly off-centre composition. All in all a great image Roger, well done   Hi Sidpixel,            I am just happy to reached the top ten, I place the spider off center for two reasons. One, it is missing a leg thus will not be ideal for composing a symmetry composition. Two, the web which supposed to compliment the spider has been disturbed thus I decided to composed it off center. Thank you so much for you detail comment, it load of help... Appreciated. Best regards, Roger New', '2017-12-11 11:10:55.000000', '2017-12-11 11:11:45.000000', 0),
(7548131, 1208800, 52549, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait of a beautiful dog. Congrats on the ribbon, Marion.</td>', 'Beautiful portrait of a beautiful dog. Congrats on the ribbon, Marion.', '2017-12-12 05:16:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548132, 1208327, 52549, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the HM, MAK. It''s a really beautiful image.</td>', 'Congrats on the HM, MAK. It''s a really beautiful image.', '2017-12-12 05:18:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548143, 1208717, 182284, '<td valign="top">Absolutely a number one pic. Awesome shot! Big congratulations!</td>', 'Absolutely a number one pic. Awesome shot! Big congratulations!', '2017-12-12 11:19:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(7548697, 1208378, 24486, '<td valign="top">Wow the voters were tough on this one, probably more shock value voting. DPC voters seen a fairly conservative group. I thought this was well captured as it looked like you had tricky lighting. Oddly enough if you had only one woman in the photograph this would probably scored much higher. This definitely wasn''t deserving any of the lower scores in my opinion</td>', 'Wow the voters were tough on this one, probably more shock value voting. DPC voters seen a fairly conservative group. I thought this was well captured as it looked like you had tricky lighting. Oddly enough if you had only one woman in the photograph this would probably scored much higher. This definitely wasn''t deserving any of the lower scores in my opinion', '2017-12-16 21:30:32.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(7548794, 1208400, 185714, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by sidpixel:</b></div><hr/><i> Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well<br/> <br/>Its truly remarkable how much is condensed into so small a space here. It gives us a fascinating insight into the density of the area especially effective at night with all the different lighting and colours. I particularly like the blurred boat on the water in the background. Thanks for shareing this man made world with us Gin. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Dear Sir<br/> <br/>Thank you so much for your comment.<br/> <br/>It is always joy to share this magnificent view with the DPC members.  <br/> <br/>cheers<br/>gin :)</td>', 'Originally posted by sidpixel: Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets contributes to the open challenge well Its truly remarkable how much is condensed into so small a space here. It gives us a fascinating insight into the density of the area especially effective at night with all the different lighting and colours. I particularly like the blurred boat on the water in the background. Thanks for shareing this man made world with us Gin.   Dear Sir Thank you so much for your comment. It is always joy to share this magnificent view with the DPC members.   cheersgin :)', '2017-12-17 21:16:37.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
